<script lang="ts">
	import Demo from "./demo.svelte";
</script>

# Resizable

Panels that share the space of a row or column, with handles between them. Drag a handle, or focus it and use the keyboard, to resize the panels beside it. Compose it from `ResizablePanelGroup`, `ResizablePanel`, and `ResizableHandle`.

<Demo />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { ResizablePanelGroup, ResizablePanel, ResizableHandle } from "#lib/components/ui/resizable/index.js";
</script>

<ResizablePanelGroup>
	<ResizablePanel defaultSize={50} minSize={20}>One</ResizablePanel>
	<ResizableHandle />
	<ResizablePanel defaultSize={50}>
		<ResizablePanelGroup direction="vertical">
			<ResizablePanel defaultSize={25}>Two</ResizablePanel>
			<ResizableHandle />
			<ResizablePanel defaultSize={75}>Three</ResizablePanel>
		</ResizablePanelGroup>
	</ResizablePanel>
</ResizablePanelGroup>
```

## Installation

```pm
npx remote0 add https://plainsv.com/r/resizable.json
```

## Sizes

Panel sizes are percentages of the group. Set `defaultSize` for the starting size; panels without one share the rest equally. Set `minSize` and `maxSize` to limit how far the handles move. A handle only resizes the two panels beside it, so the others keep their size. Use `onLayoutChange` on the group to read every size after a resize, such as to save the layout.

The group fills its container, so give the container a height for vertical groups. Panels clip content that does not fit.

## Vertical

Set `direction="vertical"` on the group to stack the panels.

<Demo section="vertical" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<ResizablePanelGroup direction="vertical">
	<ResizablePanel defaultSize={25}>Header</ResizablePanel>
	<ResizableHandle />
	<ResizablePanel defaultSize={75}>Content</ResizablePanel>
</ResizablePanelGroup>
```

## Handle

Set `withHandle` on `ResizableHandle` to show a grip in the middle of the line. The line has an 8 pixel hit area, so it is easy to grab.

<Demo section="handle" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<ResizableHandle withHandle />
```

## Disabled

Set `disabled` on `ResizableHandle` to lock it. It ignores the pointer and the arrow keys, and leaves the tab order.

<Demo section="disabled" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<ResizablePanelGroup>
	<ResizablePanel defaultSize={25}>Locked</ResizablePanel>
	<ResizableHandle withHandle disabled />
	<ResizablePanel defaultSize={50}>Content</ResizablePanel>
	<ResizableHandle withHandle />
	<ResizablePanel defaultSize={25}>Free</ResizablePanel>
</ResizablePanelGroup>
```

## Keyboard

Each handle is in the tab order and announced as a separator with the size of the panel before it. The arrow keys along the group direction move it by 5%, and Home and End move it to the panel's `minSize` and `maxSize`.

## API

`ResizablePanelGroup` and `ResizablePanel` extend the native `div` attributes, and `ResizableHandle` extends them too. The parts lay out space, so they have no `size` or `rounded` props.

```ts title="index.ts"
interface Props extends CompPropsWithChild<"div"> {
	/** `horizontal` places the panels side by side; `vertical` stacks them; defaults to `horizontal` */
	direction?: "horizontal" | "vertical";
	/** Called with every panel size, in percent and in order, after a resize */
	onLayoutChange?: (sizes: number[]) => void;
}

interface PanelProps extends CompPropsWithChild<"div"> {
	/** Starting size in percent; panels without one share the rest equally */
	defaultSize?: number;
	/** Smallest size in percent the handles allow; defaults to `0` */
	minSize?: number;
	/** Largest size in percent the handles allow; defaults to `100` */
	maxSize?: number;
}

interface HandleProps extends CompProps<"div"> {
	/** Shows a grip in the middle of the divider */
	withHandle?: boolean;
	/** Blocks resizing with this handle */
	disabled?: boolean;
}
```
